# Files copied from rsvalerio/forge, checked for drift by
# `scripts/forge-sync-check.sh` (see `make forge-sync`) against the tag
# `.github/workflows/` pins forge at.
#
# CONTRIBUTING.md stays listed even though it is a template meant to be filled
# in per repo: its permanently divergent parts are pinned by the waiver, so a
# forge-side edit to the *shared* sections still fails the check. Dropping it
# would trade a one-time waiver for a copy that silently goes stale. Editing
# this repo's copy therefore means re-recording the waiver
# (`./scripts/forge-sync-check.sh --update`), which is the intended cost.
#
# <path in this repo>   <path in rsvalerio/forge>
clippy.toml             config/clippy.toml
deny.toml               config/deny.toml
rustfmt.toml            config/rustfmt.toml
CONTRIBUTING.md         templates/CONTRIBUTING.md
